invariant: INV-26
file: aes.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: an AES=runtime QUIC object runs every block of a schedule the table
  expanded on the AES instructions, so a session whose caller's probe found
  none executes AES instructions on its Initial packets and dies of SIGILL
  on a CPU without them. The bytes do not change, because both ciphers
  keep one round-key layout, so no vector notices. bin/aes_runtime_test
  counts the calls into aes_hw.c under the absent answer and requires
  none.

--- old
    return s->instructions == CH_AES_INSTRUCTIONS_PRESENT;
--- new
    return s->instructions != 0;
